{"type":"message","id":"ae3d4f14","parentId":"7b7a209e","timestamp":"2026-05-27T07:51:33.693Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step Execution Context\n\n- Goal Run: goal-run-mpnrlu69-tbrad3\n- Step: step-01 — Update lint reference extraction so supported references are recognized from the new parser while preserving the current lint-visible behavior.\n- Stage: planner (initial)\n- Worktree: X:\\repo\\skillet\\.worktrees\\goal-move-the-lint-pipelines-p-mpnrlu69-qmv6ab\n- Goal Execution Plan: X:\\repo\\skillet\\.worktrees\\goal-move-the-lint-pipelines-p-mpnrlu69-qmv6ab\\.pi\\goal\\goal-run-mpnrlu69-tbrad3\\goal-execution-plan.json\n- Step artifact dir: X:\\repo\\skillet\\.worktrees\\goal-move-the-lint-pipelines-p-mpnrlu69-qmv6ab\\.pi\\goal\\goal-run-mpnrlu69-tbrad3\\steps\\step-01\n- Step Plan File: X:\\repo\\skillet\\.worktrees\\goal-move-the-lint-pipelines-p-mpnrlu69-qmv6ab\\.pi\\goal\\goal-run-mpnrlu69-tbrad3\\steps\\step-01\\step-plan.md\n\nGoal:\nMove the lint pipeline's Phase 2 ref extraction (in `crates/skillet/src/lint/pipeline.rs`) and the `unused_fragment` rule (in `crates/skillet/src/lint/rules/unused_fragment.rs`) to use the new parser (`crate::compiler::parse::PanParse` and `crate::compiler::PanSource`) instead of regexes.\n\nSpecifically:\n1. In `ParsedRefs::extract` (in `crates/skillet/src/refs.rs`), replace the regex-based extraction of typed refs and untyped backticks with the new parser. Parse the source using `PanSource::new` + `PanParse::new` + `parse()`, then convert `Node::Ref` to `TypedRef`, `Node::RefSuspect` to `UntypedRef` (after classification), and `Node::Fragment` can be used by the fragment rule. Keep markdown link extraction via regex since the parser doesn't handle markdown links.\n\n2. In `unused_fragment.rs`, replace the `FRAGMENT_INCLUDE_RE` regex with the parser to detect fragment inclusions.\n\n3. All existing tests must continue to pass. The lint behavior should remain identical.\n\nNote the RefKind mapping:\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Reference` → `refs::RefKind::Ref`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Path` → `refs::RefKind::Ref` (path refs are the same as ref:: for lint purposes)\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Skill` → `refs::RefKind::Skill`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Cmd` → `refs::RefKind::Cmd`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Var` → `refs::RefKind::Var`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Env` → `refs::RefKind::Env`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Agent` and `compiler::parse::RefKind::Url` — skip for now (not used by lint rules)\n\nFor `RefSuspect`, extract the text from source using the source_range (strip the outer backticks) and pass through `classify_untyped` to get the `UntypedRef`.\n\nFor fragment detection in `unused_fragment.rs`, parse each source file and collect `Node::Fragment` values.\n\nLaunching session context from the parent session.\nThis may contain clarified intent, prior planning, or constraints.\nTreat it as advisory context only.\nYou must still inspect the codebase and produce your own plan.\n\nMessage 1 • assistant\nNow let me look at the `unused_fragment` rule since it likely uses regexes to find fragment references:\n\nMessage 2 • assistant\nNow I have a clear picture. The lint pipeline's Phase 2 (`extract_refs` in `pipeline.rs`) uses the regex-based `ParsedRefs::extract` from `refs.rs`. There's a new parser in `compiler/parse.rs` that properly lexes and parses `.pan` files into `Node` types including `Ref`, `Fragment`, `RefSuspect`, etc.\n\nThe task is to move the linter to use the new parser (`compiler::parse`) instead of the regex-based approach in `refs.rs`. Let me also check what's in the `unused_fragment` rule and the compiler's lex module:\n\nMessage 3 • assistant\nNow I have a full understanding. Let me check how `ParsedRefs` is used throughout the codebase beyond the lint rules:\n\nMessage 4 • assistant\nNow I understand the full scope. The key change is in `pipeline.rs`'s `extract_refs` function and in `unused_fragment.rs`'s fragment detection. The `ParsedRefs::extract` method uses regexes — I need to replace it with the new parser. Let me also check what `compile.rs` uses (it's outside lint scope but let me note it):\n\nThe new parser produces `Node::Ref`, `Node::Fragment`, and `Node::RefSuspect` which map to the existing `TypedRef`, fragment includes, and `UntypedRef` respectively.\n\nLet me now check how the compiler's `RefKind` maps to the refs module's `RefKind`:\n\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Skill` → `refs::RefKind::Skill`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Reference` → `refs::RefKind::Ref`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Cmd` → `refs::RefKind::Cmd`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Var` → `refs::RefKind::Var`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Env` → `refs::RefKind::Env`\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Agent` → no equivalent in refs (not used by lint)\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Path` → maps to `refs::RefKind::Ref` (path refs)\n- `compiler::parse::RefKind::Url` → not used by lint currently\n\nLet me also check the `MarkdownLink` — the parser doesn't seem to handle markdown links. Let me verify:\n\nMessage 5 • assistant\nThe new parser doesn't handle markdown links — it only handles `.pan` syntax (refs, fragments, escaped bodies). So markdown links will still need the regex. Let me now look at how to approach this:\n\n1. **Replace `ParsedRefs::extract` to use the new parser** for typed refs, fragments, and untyped backticks (RefSuspect)\n2. **Keep the markdown link regex** since the parser doesn't handle markdown syntax\n3. **Replace `FRAGMENT_INCLUDE_RE` in `unused_fragment.rs`** with the parser\n\nLet me also check if `RefSuspect` gives us enough to do the untyped backtick classification:\n\nThe parser's `RefSuspect` captures backtick-wrapped text that isn't a typed ref. But we need the content to classify it. Looking at the parser, `RefSuspect` only has `source_range` — we'd need to extract the text from the source to get the content. That works.\n\nNow let me check how `PanSource` is constructed vs what we have in pipeline:\n\nMessage 6 • assistant\nGood, the compiler module is already public. Now let me implement the change:\n\n\nReturn a plan spec with these fields:\n- goal\n- summary\n- constraints[]\n- allowedFiles[]\n- implementationSteps[]\n- acceptance[] where each item has { id, kind, description, command?, required }\n\nRules:\n- acceptance must cover tests, lint, formatter checks, and regression/behavior checks that matter for this goal\n- every required criterion should have an executable command whenever feasible\n- do not omit existing-functionality checks\n- keep feedback out of prose and put the real result in the tool call"}],"timestamp":1779868293692}}
