02- \ndocs/diy-memory.md:103: **File:** `crates/skillet-compiler/src/lex.rs`\ndocs/diy-memory.md-104- \ndocs/diy-memory.md-105- ### What was built\ndocs/diy-memory.md-186- ## Stage 3 — ✅ Complete\ndocs/diy-memory.md-187- \ndocs/diy-memory.md:188: **File:** `crates/skillet-compiler/src/parse.rs`\ndocs/diy-memory.md-189- \ndocs/diy-memory.md-190- ### What was built\ndocs/diy-memory.md-190- ### What was built\ndocs/diy-memory.md-191- \ndocs/diy-memory.md:192: `PanParse<'a>` — borrows from a `PanSource` and produces a flat `Vec<Node>` plus\ndocs/diy-memory.md-193- a `Vec<ParseError>`. The parser walks the `Vec<Token>` from the lexer using a\ndocs/diy-memory.md-194- `Peekable` iterator, consuming tokens in sequence and building typed nodes.\ndocs/diy-memory.md-200- | AST shape | Flat `Vec<Node>`, not a tree | `.pan` has no nesting; a flat list is sufficient and simpler |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-201- | Ranges | On every node (`source_range: Range<u32>`) | Side-table approach would require reconstructing ranges from token spans at every diagnostic call site |\ndocs/diy-memory.md:202: | Error handling | Collect into `Vec<ParseError>`, always return `PanParse` | A linter that aborts on first error is half a linter |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-203- | Return type | `PanParse` struct (nodes + errors + path), no `Result` | Parsing always produces something useful; `Result` was a false frame |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-204- | Error message type | `ParseErrorKind` enum (not `String`) | Lets the compiler match on error kind; dynamic messages would be `String` not `Box<str>` |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-201- | Ranges | On every node (`source_range: Range<u32>`) | Side-table approach would require reconstructing ranges from token spans at every diagnostic call site |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-202- | Error handling | Collect into `Vec<ParseError>`, always return `PanParse` | A linter that aborts on first error is half a linter |\ndocs/diy-memory.md:203: | Return type | `PanParse` struct (nodes + errors + path), no `Result` | Parsing always produces something useful; `Result` was a false frame |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-204- | Error message type | `ParseErrorKind` enum (not `String`) | Lets the compiler match on error kind; dynamic messages would be `String` not `Box<str>` |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-205- | Borrow approach | `PanParse<'a>` borrows `src: &'a str` from `PanSource` | Avoids cloning; lifetime is clear; moved `get_source_string` to an `impl` method to avoid closure borrow conflicts |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-203- | Return type | `PanParse` struct (nodes + errors + path), no `Result` | Parsing always produces something useful; `Result` was a false frame |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-204- | Error message type | `ParseErrorKind` enum (not `String`) | Lets the compiler match on error kind; dynamic messages would be `String` not `Box<str>` |\ndocs/diy-memory.md:205: | Borrow approach | `PanParse<'a>` borrows `src: &'a str` from `PanSource` | Avoids cloning; lifetime is clear; moved `get_source_string` to an `impl` method to avoid closure borrow conflicts |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-206- | Recovery boundary | Advance to next `Tick` or `FragmentOpen` via `recover()` | These are the only valid entry points for structural nodes in the outer loop |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-207- | Ref parsing | `make_ref_node` helper takes `RefKind` parameter | All six ref kinds share identical token-consumption logic; only `RefKind` varies |\ndocs/diy-memory.md-229- \ndocs/diy-memory.md-230- - **`Result` vs always-succeed struct** — `Result<Vec<Node>, Vec<ParseError>>`\ndocs/diy-memory.md:231:   was the first instinct; corrected to `PanParse` because partial results and\ndocs/diy-memory.md-232-   errors coexist during error recovery.\ndocs/diy-memory.md-233- \n.pi/goal/goal-run-mpnrlu69-tbrad3/steps/orchestrator/sessions/init-r1.session-2- {\"type\":\"model_change\",\"id\":\"288d11be\",\"parentId\":null,\"timestamp\":\"2026-05-27T07:51:07.986Z\",\"provider\":\"github-copilot\",\"modelId\":\"gpt-5.4\"}\n.pi/goal/goal-run-mpnr